*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 16.67~26.67 seconds<sup>500f~800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is an exact copy of [[N-1 Grand Prix (Deadly)|N-1 Grand Prix]], though with a different restriction in place. The restriction, however, makes it ironically easier, as useful Super Rare units are much more accessible. Their disposability, combined with the generally weak peons, can easily brute force the stage.

==='''Recommended Units:'''===
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat/Bullet Train Cat]] and [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] for [[King Wahwah]] (be sure to rush the start with Maglev) to abuse his knockback.
*[[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Mohawk Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] as meatshields.
*[[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]] and [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] for chipping Wahwah.
*[[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion]] and [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island Cat]] for attacking Wahwah to exploit his high knockback count.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] for large damage towards the Roos and sometimes Wahwah. Speed talent recommended to make it easier.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] for the Shadow Boxer Ks.
*[[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] for the Scissoroos.
*[[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] for the Zang Roos.
*[[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Jamiera]] to tank multiple hits from Wahwah and the peons, his occasional wave attacks can be useful towards chipping Wahwah as well.

